    "text": "The bar chart compares the proportions of travellers booking accommodation online in North and South in 2010, 2015 and 2020. All figures are expressed as percentages.\n\nOverall, the proportion in North finished at its initial level, whereas South increased overall. North recorded the higher figure at the end of the period. The difference between the regions narrowed, from 40 percentage points in 2010 to 10 points in 2020.\n\nIn North, the figure stood at 61% in 2010, before falling to 41% five years later. It then increased to 61% in 2020. The first interval saw a change of 20 percentage points, while the corresponding movement during the second half of the decade was 20 points.\n\nSouth followed a different pattern, starting at 21% and reaching 36% in 2015. By 2020, its figure was 51%. Comparing the two regions directly, North had the larger share at the beginning, while North led at the end. The final figures of 61% for North and 51% for South therefore show a gap of 10 percentage points.",
